# Introducing Remote Execution: Decoupling[saparating] Orchestration and Execution
    Remote Execution solves the sovereignty challenge by cleanly separating where you orchestrate from where you execute. The two planes operate independently, connected only through secure outbound channels.

What is Orchestration?
    Orchestration means:
        deciding task order
        scheduling DAGs
        monitoring DAG runs
        retry logic
        dependency management

    Example:
        Task A → Task B → Task C
        Scheduler manages this.

What is Execution?
    Execution means:
        Actually running code.
    Example:
        PySpark job
        SQL query
        API call
        ML model

Astronomer divides system into 2 planes.

Plane 1: Orchestration Plane 
    Managed by Astronomer cloud.

    Contains:
    Airflow Scheduler
    Webserver
    Metadata DB
    API server

Plane 2: Execution Plane
    Customer controlled.

    Contains:
    Kubernetes cluster
    Remote agents
    Workers
    Actual data processing
    Sensitive data stays here.[Sensitive data never leaves your execution plane]

Easy Analogy
    Imagine:
    Astronomer Cloud = Manager
    Manager only says:
    "Run Task A now"
    But actual work is done inside company office.

* MOST IMPORTANT CONCEPT
    “Decoupling”
        Means: Scheduling is separated from execution
        This is the core idea of the whole chapter.

